{
  "id": "gate-control-theory",
  "term": "gate-control theory",
  "definition": "Gate-control theory is the idea that pain signals from the body can be reduced by non-painful sensory input from the same area, such as touch or mechanical stimulation. In other words, incoming pain information is partly regulated by a neural “gate,” which helps explain why actions like rubbing or massage can lessen pain.",
